## Interface: 16001
## Title: |cffC9A24ATwich|rUI Test Lab (development)
## Notes: Development tool, never part of a release: runs selected TwichUI checks inside the game and makes a report to copy. Loaded only on request.
## Author: twichie
## Version: 0.1.0-dev
## RequiredDeps: !!!TwichUI
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## X-License: MIT (code); see !!!TwichUI\LICENSE
## Category: Development

# The case registry and the case API (creates R.TestLab)
Lab.lua
# The cooperative runner (a frame with an OnUpdate only while a run is active)
Runner.lua
# The plain-text report
Report.lua
# What the window shows: pure presentation logic over the runner's records (counts, filters, search, details)
View.lua
# Reachability analysis: can a control take the pointer? (also run by the simulator scenario and the offline tests)
Reach.lua
# The guided-case mechanism: one temporary key binding, a small prompt, released when a case or the run ends
Guided.lua
# Lab-owned probe frames and the click arrangement of the client API probes (released when a case or the run ends)
Probe.lua
# Deterministic synthetic market data and the independent reference models (also loaded by tests/test_workshop_market_reference.lua)
Fixtures.lua
Reference.lua
# The cases: the same pure definitions tests/test_testlab.lua runs offline
cases\Core.lua
cases\Market.lua
cases\Crafting.lua
cases\Client.lua
cases\UI.lua
cases\Api.lua
# The window's controls, then the window (last: it opens once when the addon loads and registers /tuilab)
Kit.lua
Window.lua
